On Thu, May 15, 2014 at 11:58 AM, 'Wuzzy' via lojban <
lojban@googlegroups.com> wrote:

> Of course, the question how to say this in Lojban came up.
> Xorxes suggested =E2=80=9Cbu letteral=E2=80=9D to be lojbanized as =E2=80=
=9Czo bu zei lerfu=E2=80=9D.
> This looks strange and unintitive to me. I am not even sure if this is
> grammatical and if yes, under _which_ grammar? xD PEG? YACC? Something
> else?
>
After the Magic Words reform, which to my understanding coincided with the
writing of the PEG, {zo WORD} is a single word for purposes of word
counting. Word counting is relevant to {si}, {bu}, and {zei}, and I think
nothing else, provided we exclude experimental cmavo. This means {zo si si}
is the empty string, {zo bu zei lerfu} is a valid lujvo, and {zo bu bu} is
a valid lerfu.

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

